WEBVTT

00:06.420 --> 00:07.850
Look how far it skipped!

00:07.850 --> 00:10.150
Big news!

00:10.150 --> 00:13.110
Big news! Really big news!

00:13.330 --> 00:15.870
What's got you all worked up, Lumi?

00:18.550 --> 00:20.650
P-Pas's fiancée is here!

00:20.650 --> 00:22.540
Pas's fiancée?!

00:22.790 --> 00:25.040
Oh, Dad told me about that!

00:25.040 --> 00:27.080
He said she'll be staying here a while!

00:27.080 --> 00:29.650
A-And this fiancée...

00:29.650 --> 00:33.510
They say she's a sexy older 
woman with curves for days,

00:33.510 --> 00:36.970
and she's got Pas wrapped 
around her little finger!

00:37.370 --> 00:40.180
May I ask where we're going, Pastry?

00:40.180 --> 00:42.140
A special place.

00:42.140 --> 00:43.390
Special?

00:46.630 --> 00:49.860
Welcome to my workshop of dreams!

00:50.080 --> 00:51.410
My goodness!

01:01.380 --> 01:06.370
<i>This is the tale of a genius patissier 
who died before his time,</i>

01:06.370 --> 01:10.580
<i>and was reincarnated as the son 
of a poor noble in another world</i>

01:10.580 --> 01:13.740
<i>to pursue a world full 
of desserts and smiles.</i>

01:14.630 --> 01:19.340
<i>It's a tale that is at once cold 
and unsparing, and syrupy sweet.</i>

01:20.760 --> 01:27.140
<i>His dream is to create this 
world's very own land of sweets!</i>

01:35.030 --> 01:37.610
<b>Sweet Reincarnation</b>

02:59.550 --> 03:03.410
<b>Margravate of Hubarek  Hubarek Castle</b>

03:00.480 --> 03:03.410
My lord, are you certain of this?

03:03.880 --> 03:06.290
I understand sending Lady Petra 
to study in the royal capital

03:04.180 --> 03:10.350
<b>Sweet or Bitter? The Tea Tasting Ceremony</b>

03:06.290 --> 03:10.870
was to strengthen the trust 
of the Duke's family, but...

03:11.260 --> 03:14.340
Why send Lady Licorice 
to the Fief of Morteln?

03:14.600 --> 03:20.250
It annoys me to have that vixen 
scheming behind my back.

03:20.580 --> 03:22.970
You refer to Count Retes?

03:23.600 --> 03:24.300
Yes.

03:25.300 --> 03:29.770
It's clear that woman has designs 
on my future son-in-law.

03:30.300 --> 03:31.520
Agreed.

03:31.750 --> 03:37.830
A woman of her intelligence has surely 
grasped the Fief of Morteln's potential.

03:37.830 --> 03:41.970
And all of a sudden, she invites 
him to a tea tasting ceremony.

03:42.660 --> 03:43.950
It's all too transparent.

03:44.210 --> 03:45.580
I see.

03:45.580 --> 03:51.410
So you sent Lady Licorice to Morteln so that 
she would accompany him to the ceremony?

03:52.090 --> 03:54.100
Even for that vixen,

03:54.100 --> 03:58.300
it would prove difficult to dote on Lord 
Pastry too much with his fiancée along.

03:59.930 --> 04:00.840
And of course,

04:01.170 --> 04:06.090
there's the fatherly desire to move 
my daughter somewhere less dangerous.

04:07.590 --> 04:09.810
You think our neighbor, Lutoroute, might...

04:10.640 --> 04:13.960
I doubt they'll take news of the 
engagement between the ducal house

04:13.960 --> 04:15.460
and ours lying down.

04:17.230 --> 04:21.240
Incredible! I've never 
seen such a large kitchen!

04:21.810 --> 04:25.220
Um... may I ask what you're doing?

04:25.220 --> 04:29.700
I'm making samples for a gift I'd like 
to bring to the tea tasting party.

04:29.700 --> 04:32.860
A gift? Cookies?

04:32.860 --> 04:35.190
No, something new!

04:36.510 --> 04:37.880
Is that sugar?

04:42.450 --> 04:44.150
Those are bonkas, aren't they?

04:44.150 --> 04:45.550
And honey?

04:46.120 --> 04:48.790
They're all absolutely 
precious here in Morteln.

04:52.010 --> 04:54.820
You can only get bonkas in the royal capital.

04:55.180 --> 04:56.800
I had to give up my spending money

04:56.800 --> 05:00.800
for months in advance so 
Dad would let me have them.

05:01.740 --> 05:02.990
And what's this?

05:02.990 --> 05:04.990
You'll find out when it's done!

05:10.700 --> 05:12.190
What a sweet aroma!

05:17.820 --> 05:22.010
Incredible! The aroma just fills the room!

05:22.010 --> 05:23.090
How mysterious!

05:24.530 --> 05:25.980
This is...

05:25.980 --> 05:28.760
It's definitely a dessert 
of some kind, isn't it?

05:29.040 --> 05:31.640
Yes! Just wait and see!

05:34.660 --> 05:36.240
Yes, good.

05:36.880 --> 05:38.430
Is it finished?

05:38.430 --> 05:39.310
Oh, no.

05:39.700 --> 05:42.020
This is the hardest part.

05:47.490 --> 05:48.570
Gracious!

05:52.120 --> 05:53.740
There, there!

05:54.660 --> 05:57.840
<i>Pastry looks so excited!</i>

05:58.410 --> 06:01.000
They're so pretty and clear!

06:01.000 --> 06:03.050
They're called hard candies.

06:03.050 --> 06:04.800
Hard candies?

06:05.070 --> 06:07.170
They look like glass!

06:07.750 --> 06:10.140
And now, the finishing touches...

06:14.630 --> 06:15.610
A kitty!

06:16.190 --> 06:17.270
That's right.

06:17.270 --> 06:18.730
Lovely!

06:18.730 --> 06:19.850
And now...

06:21.890 --> 06:22.690
A doggy?

06:22.690 --> 06:23.750
Right!

06:24.170 --> 06:25.550
A bunny?

06:25.550 --> 06:26.750
Correct!

06:26.750 --> 06:27.400
And now...

06:29.450 --> 06:30.610
Um...

06:31.310 --> 06:32.830
Some sort of bird?

06:33.970 --> 06:35.790
More or less right.

06:36.570 --> 06:39.250
<i>Yeah, guess she wouldn't recognize a plane.</i>

06:41.680 --> 06:44.170
Now, how about this?

06:46.180 --> 06:47.520
Is that a flower?

06:47.520 --> 06:50.130
Yes! A peony, actually.

06:50.620 --> 06:54.360
The trick is to shape them after 
they've hardened just a bit.

06:54.360 --> 06:58.010
If they're too soft, the design 
will collapse on itself.

06:58.790 --> 07:01.350
It's crucial to get the timing just right.

07:03.000 --> 07:04.310
<i>How mysterious!</i>

07:04.930 --> 07:08.260
<i>I've seen Pastry's face wear so 
many expressions so far...</i>

07:08.570 --> 07:10.560
<i>But this one's completely new!</i>

07:11.280 --> 07:13.720
<i>So gentle and innocent...</i>

07:13.720 --> 07:16.240
<i>Yet also so confident...</i>

07:16.800 --> 07:19.200
<i>He's giving his all to his sweets!</i>

07:25.290 --> 07:26.400
Licorice?

07:28.490 --> 07:29.620
Is something the matter?

07:29.620 --> 07:31.340
Oh, no!

07:32.550 --> 07:35.700
I almost don't want to eat them...

07:35.700 --> 07:37.570
But that would be a waste!

07:39.370 --> 07:42.460
You have to eat them. 
That's what candy's for.

07:42.460 --> 07:44.510
That's true, but...

07:45.330 --> 07:48.710
They're so pretty, I just want to keep them!

07:49.690 --> 07:51.500
You silly!

07:54.250 --> 07:55.910
It's infuriating!

07:55.910 --> 07:59.570
Why won't Pas be more aggressive with her?

07:59.570 --> 08:01.500
Look at the distance he's keeping!

08:01.500 --> 08:04.210
At least put an arm around her!

08:04.210 --> 08:05.070
Hush!

08:05.070 --> 08:07.120
My lady, Lady Josephine!

08:07.120 --> 08:08.880
Pas is going to hear you!

08:09.150 --> 08:11.320
C'mon, let's knock it off.

08:11.320 --> 08:13.840
There! That's what I mean!

08:14.330 --> 08:16.520
At least hold her hand!

08:16.520 --> 08:18.310
It's getting on my nerves!

08:18.310 --> 08:21.770
Damn. Bet he's making something tasty, too!

08:23.260 --> 08:24.230
Good grief.

08:25.100 --> 08:27.040
What will you do with the bonkas?

08:27.040 --> 08:29.190
I'll do this...

08:30.200 --> 08:32.350
And coat it with the candy!

08:35.420 --> 08:37.170
They're beautiful, too!

08:37.830 --> 08:41.790
At least say, "Not one-tenth 
as beautiful as you!"

08:42.110 --> 08:43.650
Would you like to try one?

08:43.980 --> 08:45.200
May I?

08:45.200 --> 08:46.340
Of course!

08:47.470 --> 08:52.760
They say it was started as a 
method of preserving fruit.

08:53.720 --> 08:54.970
I'll try it now.

09:00.060 --> 09:01.140
It's delicious!

09:01.920 --> 09:04.600
Now get a bite of the bonka.

09:06.980 --> 09:08.060
Amazing!

09:08.450 --> 09:14.140
Isn't the tart bonka flavor so refreshing 
after your tongue adjusts to the sweetness?

09:14.140 --> 09:15.180
Yes!

09:16.010 --> 09:20.190
That delicate balance is this 
dessert's greatest appeal!

09:20.750 --> 09:25.010
It's delicious in a different way 
than just eating the bonka, too.

09:25.420 --> 09:27.040
How mysterious!

09:27.540 --> 09:28.420
Now, then...

09:34.190 --> 09:35.420
That hurt!

09:35.420 --> 09:37.430
What are you doing, Pas?!

09:37.430 --> 09:40.650
I should be asking why 
<i>you all</i> are here, Sister.

09:40.650 --> 09:42.890
What? Oh... I...

09:42.890 --> 09:44.530
Not to mention you, Mother!

09:45.210 --> 09:47.030
I have business to attend to!

09:47.030 --> 09:48.720
Let's hurry, Mother!

09:48.720 --> 09:51.300
Take care, Licorice!

09:52.360 --> 09:53.530
My lady!

09:53.530 --> 09:55.380
Lady Josephine, wait!

09:55.380 --> 09:57.400
Eavesdropping is not a nice habit.

09:57.400 --> 09:58.930
They hung us out to dry!

09:58.930 --> 10:02.330
Damn it! You can't trust grown-ups!

10:02.710 --> 10:06.180
I was going to let you two 
sample them too, but...

10:06.180 --> 10:07.540
Can we eat them?!

10:07.540 --> 10:08.790
Heck yeah!

10:10.690 --> 10:13.680
In light of your eavesdropping, 
I'm calling that off.

10:17.120 --> 10:20.220
I'll give them to Father and Feuille instead.

10:20.220 --> 10:22.680
Aw, no!

10:26.730 --> 10:28.890
I hope it'll be all right...

10:30.270 --> 10:31.100
What will?

10:31.100 --> 10:33.600
The kid's bodyguard.

10:33.600 --> 10:37.160
You think a newbie like 
Nicolo can really handle it?

10:37.470 --> 10:42.320
The count's tea tastings draw young, 
marriageable nobles from all over the south.

10:42.680 --> 10:45.350
It's a social gathering for matchmaking.

10:45.870 --> 10:48.290
It's not a place for you or I.

10:48.800 --> 10:52.250
Still, this is Count 
Retes we're dealing with!

10:52.520 --> 10:55.800
Yeah, and Pas can handle himself.

10:56.180 --> 10:58.720
It's Licorice I'm more worried about.

10:59.590 --> 11:01.980
Caera will be with her,

11:01.980 --> 11:05.180
but she doesn't seem very comfortable 
with social situations.

11:05.700 --> 11:08.510
I hope that vixen won't try to humiliate her.

11:10.500 --> 11:13.270
<i>I'm counting on you, Pas.</i>

11:23.530 --> 11:25.410
Look at all those people!

11:25.800 --> 11:29.010
And the decorations in the great hall...

11:29.010 --> 11:31.120
This is even more impressive 
than the royal capital!

11:31.420 --> 11:34.680
Yes... it truly is an impressive room.

11:34.680 --> 11:38.650
Retesvale Castle is known as one of 
the greatest castles in the south.

11:39.020 --> 11:43.590
It's also called "Pirate Castle" 
for its proximity to the ocean.

11:44.610 --> 11:46.560
Pirate Castle...

11:47.980 --> 11:49.410
Pastry?

11:49.410 --> 11:51.520
Look at all those chandeliers...

11:52.090 --> 11:55.800
How many casks of sugar could I buy 
with the money spent to buy them?

11:58.120 --> 12:00.000
O-Oh, nothing!

12:00.000 --> 12:01.450
Lord Pastry.

12:01.910 --> 12:04.870
You <i>are</i> the lady's escort, remember.

12:04.870 --> 12:07.180
Please maintain your attention.

12:07.180 --> 12:09.090
D-Do forgive me.

12:09.090 --> 12:10.660
I'm sorry, Licorice.

12:11.150 --> 12:12.410
Scary!

12:14.450 --> 12:15.380
Is that...

12:15.860 --> 12:17.740
the picture I made?

12:19.770 --> 12:22.550
<i>I didn't expect her to set it out here.</i>

12:23.450 --> 12:25.420
<i>It almost feels intentional...</i>

12:25.420 --> 12:26.510
Well, well!

12:26.980 --> 12:29.420
If it isn't Lord Pastry Morteln.

12:29.420 --> 12:31.730
You are most welcome here.

12:33.110 --> 12:36.690
I was most honored by the invitation.

12:37.290 --> 12:38.150
Not at all.

12:38.150 --> 12:43.370
Her Ladyship told me to show 
you only the greatest respect.

12:43.370 --> 12:44.150
And...

12:44.650 --> 12:48.370
to keep a close eye on you as well.

12:48.630 --> 12:50.940
<i>I guess they're afraid 
of me causing trouble.</i>

12:51.430 --> 12:54.330
Well, let's maintain a spirit of cordiality!

12:54.330 --> 12:56.170
Most agreed.

12:56.170 --> 13:01.300
<i>This is my big chance to promote the 
Fief of Morteln's specialties, anyway.</i>

13:01.790 --> 13:06.240
This is my fiancée, Licorice Mille Hubarek.

13:07.610 --> 13:13.770
She's never been to a gathering of 
southern nobles, so she accompanied me.

13:14.120 --> 13:16.730
It is my pleasure to make your acquaintance.

13:17.220 --> 13:19.690
My name is Coaton Engels.

13:20.250 --> 13:22.900
Attention, all! I wish 
to make an introduction.

13:23.180 --> 13:25.210
Invited here by our house,

13:25.210 --> 13:27.560
Lord Pastry Mille Morteln

13:27.560 --> 13:30.080
and his fiancée, Lady Licorice!

13:31.330 --> 13:32.830
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

13:33.570 --> 13:35.370
My name is Pastry.

13:35.370 --> 13:37.160
Young though I may be,

13:37.160 --> 13:38.790
I hope you will greet me with open arms.

13:42.180 --> 13:44.270
As a token of our acquaintance,

13:44.650 --> 13:46.970
I've brought a gift.

13:47.220 --> 13:49.260
I believe it will go well with the tea.

13:49.260 --> 13:50.880
How beautiful!

13:50.880 --> 13:52.350
Are they artisanal goods?

13:52.350 --> 13:53.930
It's called "hard candy."

13:53.930 --> 13:56.640
Candy? It's edible, then?

13:56.990 --> 13:59.100
By all means, help yourselves!

14:05.410 --> 14:06.820
Th-This is...

14:07.030 --> 14:08.900
It melts in my mouth!

14:08.900 --> 14:12.280
It's like happiness itself 
soaking into my tongue!

14:14.100 --> 14:15.790
Have one for yourself, Sir Coaton.

14:16.250 --> 14:18.420
As you wish.

14:21.090 --> 14:22.670
I-Incredible!

14:24.540 --> 14:26.580
<i>It's like a torrent of sweetness!</i>

14:26.580 --> 14:29.930
<i>Yet it's so rich and full!</i>

14:30.280 --> 14:33.640
<i>Such a sweet, gentle aroma 
filling my nostrils...</i>

14:35.710 --> 14:37.550
It goes well with the tea.

14:37.550 --> 14:42.030
Truly, the sweets and the tea 
leaves play a perfect harmony.

14:42.030 --> 14:45.070
I-I didn't expect you to 
be a poet, Sir Coaton.

14:46.300 --> 14:48.780
It brings out the flavor 
of the tea even more!

14:49.330 --> 14:51.740
We made a number of samples.

14:52.060 --> 14:54.770
And now that we're all friends,

14:54.770 --> 14:58.710
I'd love to send you more by 
way of traveling merchants!

14:59.100 --> 15:00.590
You would do that?

15:00.590 --> 15:01.420
Of course.

15:01.420 --> 15:03.570
And as they're gifts, you don't have to pay.

15:03.570 --> 15:05.650
You're certain?

15:05.650 --> 15:07.380
Yes, although...

15:08.130 --> 15:10.550
In that case, might I ask that

15:10.550 --> 15:14.720
the merchants in question not 
be subject to sugar taxes?

15:15.290 --> 15:16.930
Not subject to taxes?

15:17.240 --> 15:19.880
Sugary goods are taxed very highly.

15:19.880 --> 15:21.550
Since the amount is so small,

15:21.550 --> 15:26.660
having them taxed every time I send 
them wouldn't be fair to the merchants.

15:27.000 --> 15:31.860
Well... it <i>would</i> seem a bit odd 
to apply taxes to a gift.

15:31.860 --> 15:32.860
I see...

15:34.660 --> 15:36.790
What an interesting proposal.

15:40.210 --> 15:43.040
I'd <i>love</i> to hear more about it.

15:43.540 --> 15:46.130
Thank you for coming today, everyone.

15:46.130 --> 15:47.830
Count Retes.

15:47.830 --> 15:49.710
I was honored to receive your invitation.

15:50.070 --> 15:52.680
And would this be your lovely fiancée?

15:54.110 --> 15:56.140
It is a pleasure to meet you!

15:58.130 --> 16:01.920
I'd love to hear more of what 
you were proposing just now.

16:02.300 --> 16:06.150
I really do prefer all business 
matters to go through me first.

16:06.150 --> 16:09.610
Oh, not at all. We're merely 
talking about personal gifts.

16:10.210 --> 16:12.070
Shall we speak in private?

16:12.410 --> 16:13.560
Gladly.

16:14.790 --> 16:18.740
Would the lady care to wait here, then?

16:20.810 --> 16:25.310
It concerns negotiations between my 
household and House Morteln, after all.

16:27.270 --> 16:30.890
Coaton, show our guests 
only the greatest respect.

16:30.890 --> 16:31.670
Milady.

16:32.640 --> 16:34.100
I'll return soon.

16:34.100 --> 16:35.520
All right...

16:39.500 --> 16:41.020
It'll be fine.

16:41.800 --> 16:43.830
Look after Licorice, would you?

16:43.830 --> 16:45.040
We will.

16:45.040 --> 16:46.410
We shall.

16:54.270 --> 16:56.820
This is all very intimidating!

16:56.820 --> 16:59.780
I am the leader of the 
County of Retes, after all.

16:59.780 --> 17:02.750
Do you feel I'm going to 
hurt you, Your Ladyship?

17:03.010 --> 17:07.180
If I did, I would have prepared 
ten times the number of guards.

17:07.180 --> 17:11.360
A handful of guards would be 
nothing before a magic-user.

17:12.170 --> 17:14.840
And I'm merely a frail woman, after all.

17:14.840 --> 17:17.770
Surely it's important that 
I be as cautious as I can?

17:18.280 --> 17:20.850
<i>You don't look especially frail to me.</i>

17:21.110 --> 17:23.070
Now, regarding our discussion from before.

17:23.380 --> 17:26.810
Let's get right to business. No more games.

17:27.670 --> 17:28.770
What do you want?

17:29.680 --> 17:31.980
<i>I can't talk my way around her.</i>

17:40.250 --> 17:42.790
First, try one of these.

17:43.540 --> 17:45.450
Is this a cow, perhaps?

17:45.450 --> 17:46.000
Try it.

17:49.720 --> 17:50.920
How is it?

17:51.450 --> 17:53.240
<i>A sophisticated flavor.</i>

17:53.240 --> 17:54.810
<i>Sweet, but not cloying.</i>

17:55.320 --> 17:57.820
<i>I've eaten many tea sweets in my time,</i>

17:57.820 --> 18:00.930
<i>but this transparent sweet 
is truly worthy of praise!</i>

18:01.460 --> 18:02.890
It's quite delicious.

18:03.400 --> 18:04.920
Thank you for saying that.

18:05.450 --> 18:07.350
I made it myself.

18:07.690 --> 18:10.850
And this flavoring... honey?

18:10.850 --> 18:14.140
Very impressive! You could tell?

18:14.140 --> 18:17.570
It's made from water, sugar, and honey.

18:18.230 --> 18:20.030
Surprisingly simple, then.

18:20.390 --> 18:24.990
I hope to some day produce all 
the ingredients in our fief.

18:24.990 --> 18:26.710
All the ingredients?

18:26.710 --> 18:30.460
You mean to produce honey and 
sugar in the Fief of Morteln?

18:30.780 --> 18:36.440
Yes, I expect to be able to mass 
produce these candies within three years.

18:36.890 --> 18:39.390
<i>On that barren plot of land?</i>

18:41.320 --> 18:45.100
<i>No... knowing him, he might just do it.</i>

18:46.030 --> 18:49.150
And as Your Ladyship has access to a harbor,

18:49.150 --> 18:51.690
I was hoping I might have your 
support in this endeavor.

18:51.690 --> 18:54.460
I just used a roundabout 
approach to get there.

18:54.460 --> 18:58.260
Hence all your talk of taxes?

18:58.260 --> 18:59.610
Yes, well observed.

18:59.990 --> 19:06.080
<i>Heavens. It doesn't seem possible, 
but could his end goal be...</i>

19:06.080 --> 19:08.970
<i>Something greater... much further ahead?</i>

19:09.550 --> 19:12.040
<i>Just what kind of future is he seeking?</i>

19:12.290 --> 19:13.560
Very well.

19:13.560 --> 19:18.760
I'll give you what aid I can, 
but only as regards these candies.

19:19.850 --> 19:21.470
Thank you so much!

19:21.470 --> 19:25.930
<i>That future of yours... 
I'll put it in my own pocket.</i>

19:26.740 --> 19:29.420
By the way... what is this?

19:31.150 --> 19:34.600
Lord Pastry is seems to 
be the talk of the party!

19:34.600 --> 19:35.360
What?

19:35.660 --> 19:40.320
He'll certainly come away 
with many new admirers.

19:42.000 --> 19:48.050
I'm sure he'll foster quite a few new 
relationships from this occasion.

19:48.050 --> 19:49.630
It's quite enviable.

19:50.990 --> 19:55.210
<i>Pastry... with other women?</i>

19:55.780 --> 19:57.940
If you'll excuse me.

19:58.860 --> 20:03.260
Lord Pastry is so young, 
but he's very refined, isn't he?

20:03.260 --> 20:05.890
Milady. Ignore them.

20:05.890 --> 20:07.920
And that wonderful smile!

20:07.920 --> 20:10.310
She's right. Don't listen.

20:10.310 --> 20:13.930
Did you hear? Lord Pastry's fiancée...

20:13.930 --> 20:17.030
She's the daughter of Margrave Hubarek!

20:17.860 --> 20:20.550
My! That prestigious family in the east?

20:21.980 --> 20:22.820
Milady!

20:23.070 --> 20:27.310
<i>I'm really not... comfortable 
in situations like this.</i>

20:27.640 --> 20:31.730
<i>I came because I thought Pastry 
would be with me, but...</i>

20:31.730 --> 20:34.240
Can I get you something to drink?

20:34.240 --> 20:36.190
I want to go home!

20:38.070 --> 20:40.140
It's quite a pleasure 
doing business with you.

20:40.580 --> 20:42.010
The pleasure is all mine.

20:42.430 --> 20:46.910
<i>Count Retes's mercantile connections 
are the greatest in the south.</i>

20:46.910 --> 20:49.350
<i>Having her backing is more 
than I could hope for!</i>

20:49.730 --> 20:52.900
<i>I'm one step closer to 
mass-producing hard candy!</i>

20:53.690 --> 20:56.470
And that charming fiancée of yours...

20:57.690 --> 21:01.440
I hear you protected her 
during the kidnapping.

21:01.440 --> 21:02.900
Y-Yes...

21:03.270 --> 21:05.860
Licorice... I hope she's all right.

21:05.860 --> 21:09.870
I'm sure she fell for you 
after how you impressed her.

21:10.330 --> 21:11.840
I'm not certain it was quite—

21:11.840 --> 21:15.870
And she's a fine match for 
the next Lord of Morteln.

21:16.220 --> 21:20.340
No man could complain at having 
Licorice for a partner.

21:20.610 --> 21:23.050
She's very charming.

21:23.330 --> 21:25.010
Gracious!

21:25.010 --> 21:27.720
So precocious! You're as 
flustered as a grown man.

21:27.720 --> 21:29.480
I-I'm not flustered...

21:29.480 --> 21:30.890
You love her, don't you?

21:30.890 --> 21:33.060
Th-This is hardly the time or place to—

21:33.060 --> 21:35.520
Just admit you love her!

21:35.940 --> 21:37.830
Y-Your Ladyship?!

21:38.200 --> 21:42.080
I won't release you until you 
admit your true feelings!

21:42.080 --> 21:44.240
Th-This is highly inappropriate!

21:52.080 --> 21:53.270
Lico—

23:37.130 --> 23:39.030
Next time on <i>Sweet Reincarnation</i>...

23:39.080 --> 23:44.980
<b>Apples of Love and Sad Threats of War</b>

23:39.360 --> 23:41.890
"Apples of Love and Sad Threats of War."

23:41.890 --> 23:43.320
Bon appétit!

23:44.980 --> 23:50.250
<b>Illustration:</b>

23:44.980 --> 23:50.250
<b>Kabocha</b>
